THE UNIFORM TITLE INSURANCE POLICY

THIS POLICY is issued by [Company Name], a duly authorized title insurance company, to the insured, Andrée J. Boucher, whose address is 1729 Jeremy Lock, Apt. 2399.

The Company insures the insured against loss or damage, not exceeding the amount of the policy, as a result of:

1. Title being vested otherwise than as stated in the policy;
2. Any defect in or lien or encumbrance on the title;
3. Unmarketability of the title;
4. Lack of a right of access to and from the land;
5. Any lien or encumbrance for real estate taxes or assessments not shown in the public records;
6. Any failure to comply with the conditions of any variance, building line, zoning or similar ordinance or regulation affecting the land;
7. Any claim by any person, other than a named excluded person, resulting from the invalidity or unenforceability of the insured mortgage, based on usury or any consumer protection statute.

The Company will pay the amount of the policy upon proof of loss or damage.

This policy does not insure against:

1. Loss or damage caused by:
  a. Use or encumbrance of the land before the date of the policy;
  b. Easements, liens or encumbrances, or any other defects, not shown in the public records;
2. Any claim, by reason of the operation of federal, state or local statutes or regulations, resulting in loss or damage, not excluded herein;
3. Any claim, by reason of the breach of any covenant, condition or agreement contained in any instrument creating the insured mortgage, except as provided in Section 5 of the Conditions;
4. Any claim, by reason of any defect in or lien or encumbrance on the title caused by:
  a. The insured's failure to pay any sums when due;
  b. The insured's acts or omissions;
